      "text": "Geometric mean is the nth root of the product of the numbers.  Thus, $$\n\\sqrt{xy} = \\sqrt{3} \\implies xy = 3,\n$$\nwhich means the two numbers $a$ and $b$ satisfy $$\na \\cdot b = xy = 3.\n$$  Similarly,\n$$\n\\frac{a+b}{2} = \\frac{3}{2}, \\qquad \\Rightarrow \\qquad a+b = 3.\n$$  Thus, if $a$ and $b$ are the two unknown numbers, then we have\n$$\na \\cdot b = 3, \\qquad a + b = 3.\n$$  Solving these equations gives $$\n\\begin{aligned}\na^2 - ab + b^2 &= 0 \\\\\n(a-b)^2 &= 0 \\\\\na &= b.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nIf $a=b$, then $b^2 = 3$, so $$\nb = \\sqrt{3} \\quad \\text{or} \\quad b = -\\sqrt{3}.\n$$  Both are positive, so the answer is $$\n\\boxed{\\sqrt{3}, \\sqrt{3}}.\n$$",
